==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=takedown}}

===Etymology===
A bare nominalization of the verb {{term|take down|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|lang=en}} A [[take down|taking down]]: the [[arrest]] of a suspect by a police officer.
# {{context|martial arts|lang=en}} A [[take down|taking down]]: an act of bringing one's opponent to the ground by grabbing one or both legs and applying a rearward bending moment.
#* {{projectlink|pedia|Takedown (grappling)}}
# Enforced removal of material from a [[website]], etc.
#* '''2001''', Charles H. Kennedy, ''An introduction to U.S. telecommunications law''
#*: The DMCA also gives the targets of notice-and-'''takedown''' complaints a limited opportunity to have access to their materials restored.

